  "content_html": "<div id=\"topic-title\">\n    <h1>\n      <a href=\"/t/dickover-in-the-slashdot-rss-feed/372\">Dickover in the Slashdot RSS feed</a>\n    </h1>\n\n      <div class=\"topic-category\" itemscope itemtype=\"http://schema.org/BreadcrumbList\">\n          <span itemprop=\"itemListElement\" itemscope itemtype=\"http://schema.org/ListItem\">\n            <a href=\"/c/app/6\" class=\"badge-wrapper bullet\" itemprop=\"item\">\n              <span class='badge-category-bg'></span>\n              <span class='badge-category clear-badge'>\n                <span class='category-name' itemprop='name'>App</span>\n              </span>\n            </a>\n            <meta itemprop=\"position\" content=\"1\" />\n          </span>\n      </div>\n\n  </div>\n\n  \n\n    <div itemscope=\"itemscope\" itemtype=\"http://schema.org/DiscussionForumPosting\">\n      <meta itemprop='headline' content='Dickover in the Slashdot RSS feed'>\n      <link itemprop='url' href='https://discourse.netnewswire.com/t/dickover-in-the-slashdot-rss-feed/372'>\n      <meta itemprop='datePublished' content='2026-09-06T04:45:58Z'>\n      <meta itemprop='keywords' content=''>\n          <meta itemprop='articleSection' content='App'>\n        <div itemprop='publisher' itemscope itemtype=\"http://schema.org/Organization\">\n          <meta itemprop='name' content='NetNewsWire'>\n        </div>\n\n\n\n          <div id='post_1'  class='topic-body crawler-post'>\n            <div class='crawler-post-meta'>\n              <span class=\"creator\" itemprop=\"author\" itemscope=\"itemscope\" itemtype=\"http://schema.org/Person\">\n                <a rel='nofollow' href='https://discourse.netnewswire.com/u/Joerg'><span itemprop=\"name\">Joerg</span></a>\n                  <meta itemprop='url' content='https://discourse.netnewswire.com/u/Joerg'>\n                \n              </span>\n\n                <link itemprop=\"mainEntityOfPage\" href=\"https://discourse.netnewswire.com/t/dickover-in-the-slashdot-rss-feed/372\">\n\n                <link itemprop=\"image\" href=\"https://discourse.netnewswire.com/uploads/default/original/1X/f611e834ffd073379ee699da09ae40eb43e250bf.png\">\n\n              <span class=\"crawler-post-infos\">\n                  <time  datetime='2026-09-06T04:45:58Z' class='post-time'>\n                    September 6, 2026,  4:45am\n                  </time>\n                  <meta itemprop='dateModified' content='2026-09-06T04:45:58Z'>\n              <span itemprop=\"position\">1</span>\n              </span>\n            </div>\n            <div class='post' itemprop=\"text\">\n              <p>Since a couple of weeks I see a cookie banner presented in the slashdot feed. I don‘t think I have ever seen something like that in an RSS feed before and I‘m unsure if this is a bug or if NNW can do something about it. Because it somehow interrupts the flow. <img src=\"https://discourse.netnewswire.com/images/emoji/twitter/nerd_face.png?v=15\" title=\":nerd_face:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":nerd_face:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>The feed URL: <a href=\"http://rss.slashdot.org/Slashdot/slashdotMain\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Slashdot</a></p>\n<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://discourse.netnewswire.com/uploads/default/original/1X/f611e834ffd073379ee699da09ae40eb43e250bf.png\" data-download-href=\"https://discourse.netnewswire.com/uploads/default/f611e834ffd073379ee699da09ae40eb43e250bf\" title=\"IMG_0330\"><img src=\"https://discourse.netnewswire.com/uploads/default/optimized/1X/f611e834ffd073379ee699da09ae40eb43e250bf_2_690x453.png\" alt=\"IMG_0330\" data-base62-sha1=\"z6PP3fF5mowVEUNq14dHFVepqj5\" width=\"690\" height=\"453\" srcset=\"https://discourse.netnewswire.com/uploads/default/optimized/1X/f611e834ffd073379ee699da09ae40eb43e250bf_2_690x453.png, https://discourse.netnewswire.com/uploads/default/optimized/1X/f611e834ffd073379ee699da09ae40eb43e250bf_2_1035x679.png 1.5x, https://discourse.netnewswire.com/uploads/default/optimized/1X/f611e834ffd073379ee699da09ae40eb43e250bf_2_1380x906.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"989C9E\"><div class=\"meta\"><span class=\"filename\">IMG_0330</span><span class=\"informations\">2266×1488 625 KB</span></div></a></div></p>\n            </div>\n\n              <div itemprop=\"interactionStatistic\" itemscope=\"itemscope\" itemtype=\"http://schema.org/InteractionCounter\">\n                  <meta itemprop=\"interactionType\" content=\"http://schema.org/LikeAction\"/>\n                  <meta itemprop=\"userInteractionCount\" content=\"0\" />\n                <span class='post-likes'></span>\n              </div>\n\n\n            \n\n\n          </div>\n          <div id='post_2' itemprop=\"comment\" itemscope=\"itemscope\" itemtype=\"http://schema.org/Comment\" class='topic-body crawler-post'>\n            <div class='crawler-post-meta'>\n              <span class=\"creator\" itemprop=\"author\" itemscope=\"itemscope\" itemtype=\"http://schema.org/Person\">\n                <a rel='nofollow' href='https://discourse.netnewswire.com/u/buchb'><span itemprop=\"name\">buchb</span></a>\n                  <meta itemprop='url' content='https://discourse.netnewswire.com/u/buchb'>\n                \n              </span>\n\n\n\n              <span class=\"crawler-post-infos\">\n                  <time itemprop=\"datePublished\" datetime='2026-09-06T13:49:42Z' class='post-time'>\n                    September 6, 2026,  1:49pm\n                  </time>\n                  <meta itemprop='dateModified' content='2026-09-06T13:49:42Z'>\n              <span itemprop=\"position\">2</span>\n              </span>\n            </div>\n            <div class='post' itemprop=\"text\">\n              <p>Looks like it’s loading the actual website, probably in an iframe</p>\n            </div>\n\n              <div itemprop=\"interactionStatistic\" itemscope=\"itemscope\" itemtype=\"http://schema.org/InteractionCounter\">\n                  <meta itemprop=\"interactionType\" content=\"http://schema.org/LikeAction\"/>\n                  <meta itemprop=\"userInteractionCount\" content=\"0\" />\n                <span class='post-likes'></span>\n              </div>\n\n\n            \n\n\n          </div>\n          <div id='post_3' itemprop=\"comment\" itemscope=\"itemscope\" itemtype=\"http://schema.org/Comment\" class='topic-body crawler-post'>\n            <div class='crawler-post-meta'>\n              <span class=\"creator\" itemprop=\"author\" itemscope=\"itemscope\" itemtype=\"http://schema.org/Person\">\n                <a rel='nofollow' href='https://discourse.netnewswire.com/u/brent'><span itemprop=\"name\">brent</span></a>\n                  <meta itemprop='url' content='https://discourse.netnewswire.com/u/brent'>\n                \n              </span>\n\n\n\n              <span class=\"crawler-post-infos\">\n                  <time itemprop=\"datePublished\" datetime='2026-09-06T15:26:53Z' class='post-time'>\n                    September 6, 2026,  3:26pm\n                  </time>\n                  <meta itemprop='dateModified' content='2026-09-06T15:26:53Z'>\n              <span itemprop=\"position\">3</span>\n              </span>\n            </div>\n            <div class='post' itemprop=\"text\">\n              <p>Which version of NetNewsWire are you using? In NetNewsWire 7.1.3 we added some code to prevent this from Slashdot.</p>\n<p>(It’s possible that they’ve changed their HTML so that our fix no longer works, of course.)</p>\n            </div>\n\n              <div itemprop=\"interactionStatistic\" itemscope=\"itemscope\" itemtype=\"http://schema.org/InteractionCounter\">\n                  <meta itemprop=\"interactionType\" content=\"http://schema.org/LikeAction\"/>\n                  <meta itemprop=\"userInteractionCount\" content=\"0\" />\n                <span class='post-likes'></span>\n              </div>\n\n\n            \n\n\n          </div>\n          <div id='post_4' itemprop=\"comment\" itemscope=\"itemscope\" itemtype=\"http://schema.org/Comment\" class='topic-body crawler-post'>\n            <div class='crawler-post-meta'>\n              <span class=\"creator\" itemprop=\"author\" itemscope=\"itemscope\" itemtype=\"http://schema.org/Person\">\n                <a rel='nofollow' href='https://discourse.netnewswire.com/u/Joerg'><span itemprop=\"name\">Joerg</span></a>\n                  <meta itemprop='url' content='https://discourse.netnewswire.com/u/Joerg'>\n                \n              </span>\n\n\n\n              <span class=\"crawler-post-infos\">\n                  <time itemprop=\"datePublished\" datetime='2026-09-06T16:42:25Z' class='post-time'>\n                    September 6, 2026,  4:42pm\n                  </time>\n                  <meta itemprop='dateModified' content='2026-09-06T16:42:25Z'>\n              <span itemprop=\"position\">4</span>\n              </span>\n            </div>\n            <div class='post' itemprop=\"text\">\n              <p>It‘s the current Testflight Build 7210. I noticed that the message doesn‘t pop up on every new article. Kind of odd.</p>\n            </div>\n\n              <div itemprop=\"interactionStatistic\" itemscope=\"itemscope\" itemtype=\"http://schema.org/InteractionCounter\">\n                  <meta itemprop=\"interactionType\" content=\"http://schema.org/LikeAction\"/>\n                  <meta itemprop=\"userInteractionCount\" content=\"0\" />\n                <span class='post-likes'></span>\n              </div>\n\n\n            \n\n\n          </div>\n\n    </div>",
